# Data and large artifacts (under Desktop/OncoTox/data; see scripts/layout.py)
# Anchored with a leading slash: unanchored, `data/` also matched notebooks/outputs/data/,
# whose figures and tables are meant to be committed (10.08.2026).
/data/

# Python bytecode and caches
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so

# Virtual environments
.venv/
venv/
env/

# Packaging / build
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/
*.egg

# Jupyter
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# Test / type / lint caches
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# IDE and OS
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*~
.DS_Store

# AnnData / embedding outputs (if written under the repo tree)
*.h5ad

# Training run artifacts (checkpoints, configs, histories, per-drug results).
# The runs_index.csv ledger is committed by hand if you ever want to share it.
runs/

# personal presentation material (speaker notes + evidence appendix)
docs/progress_report_*.md

# LaTeX build artifacts. main.pdf is one of them: it was tracked until 10.08.2026 and went
# stale whenever a .tex changed without a rebuild. Build it with
#     pdflatex main.tex && bibtex main && pdflatex main.tex && pdflatex main.tex
# Corrected 12.08.2026: this said "pdflatex main.tex twice", which is not enough. The report uses
# plain bibtex (report/sections/07_bibliography.tex), and main.bbl is ignored below -- so in a fresh
# clone or git worktree, pdflatex-twice emits 33 undefined citations and a bibliography-free PDF.
# It appears to work in a tree that has been built before only because a stale main.bbl is lying
# around. Found by building the report in a worktree and reading the log rather than the page count.
# project_planning_v2.pdf stays tracked -- it is a source document, not a build product.
report/main.pdf
report/*.aux
report/*.log
report/*.out
report/*.toc
report/*.fls
report/*.fdb_latexmk
report/*.synctex.gz
report/*.bbl
report/*.blg
